{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/807475-ghoul-blood-addiction-vs-dominate","id":807475,"title":"Ghoul/Blood addiction vs Dominate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T18:02:24-08:00","id":807475,"title":"Ghoul/Blood addiction vs Dominate","content":"Which one wins out when a Domitor calls on a ghoul to do something. if said ghoul has been dominated by a separate vampire?<br /> <br /> For instance. a Ghoul is told by Domitor NOT to go near or associate with a particular vampire. when said Vampire has gotten tot he ghoul and dominated it to remain where it is with said Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:30:03-08:00","id":807519,"title":"","content":"I think you mean blood bond, not blood addiction. Vitae addiction is just a drug addiction, with a focus on vitae instead of cocaine or tobacco. Blood bond is the actual mind affecting stuff.<br /> <br /> Dominate wins, hands down. The Vinculum does three things - 1) gives a Perfect impression, 2) Integrity check to hurt Dominus, and 3) +X Discipline dice bonus. In truth, someone can simply ignore their Dominator (social maneuvering can't force you to do some things, and Integrity checks aren't impassible barrier) and do whatever they want if they pay the cost. True, the emotional fallout is hell, but its technically possible.<br /> <br /> Dominate bypasses all that free will stuff and goes right to forcing someone to do it. Same with Majesty and Nightmare. Auspex makes people think they want to do whatever by inserting thoughts into their brain, so theoretically can disobey the Dominus &quot;of their own free will.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Vinculum is a powerful tool. Its not an unbeatable tool, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:38:34-08:00","id":807526,"title":"","content":"The only protection against Dominate that blood bonding provides is that harming the Regnant/Domitor is a breaking point. Ordering a thrall to do something they believe will harm their Regnant may snap them out of it. That said, something as vague as breaking an order to &quot;not talk to this guy&quot; probably wouldn't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:48:30-08:00","id":807573,"title":"","content":"Dominate wins in most situations. If the Dominator is looking to have the bonded target harm the regent, then that triggers breaking points. Breaing points end some Dominate effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T22:46:06-08:00","id":807628,"title":"","content":"I agree that the Dominate would win here, but a command that would hurt the Regant gives the normal chance to snap out of it.<br /> <br /> That being said, if the Regnant too has used Dominate, I would give the Vinculum Discipline bonus on the Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T03:44:25-08:00","id":807760,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, definitely. Dominate &gt; Vinculum, but Dominate + Vinculum &gt; Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}